  happyWinter:
  - speaker: 
    text: The plant withered, petal by petal, and the wolf, being free from the control
      of the bloom, ran into the trees.
  - speaker: 
    text: I applied first aid and carried my daughter home. She stayed asleep the
      entire time.
  - speaker: 
    text: Hollow Pine was allowed a calm winter, knowing the plant was eradicated.
  - speaker: 
    text: I gained a pat on the back, some handshakes, and a lot of booze.
  - speaker: 
    text: But my daughter gave me a smile.
  - speaker: 
    text: A genuine one.
  - speaker: 
    text: The same one she used to give her mother.
  - speaker: 
    text: I started crying on the spot.
  - speaker: 
    text: Yes, yes... I know. Everyone made fun of me too.
  - speaker: 
    text: But it was all for that.
  - speaker: 
    text: To protect that smile.
  - speaker: 
    text: The best reward I could've ever received.
  happyWinterWithLoss:
  - speaker: 
    text: The plant withered, petal by petal, and the wolf, being free from the control
      of the bloom, ran into the trees.
  - speaker: 
    text: I applied first aid and carried my daughter home. She stayed asleep the
      entire time.
  - speaker: 
    text: Eventually, the plants fell off, and everyone looked healthier than ever.
  - speaker: 
    text: Hollow Pine was allowed a calm winter, knowing the plant was eradicated,
      but some of the townsfolk would never come back.
  - speaker: 
    text: I could've done something differently... I let one of them get away, or
      I shot something I shouldn't have. I knew it.
  - speaker: 
    text: But while drowning in sorrow and booze, I gained a pat on the back, some
      handshakes, and a genuine smile from my daughter.
  - speaker: 
    text: And I remembered why I did everything.
  - speaker: 
    text: All for that.
  - speaker: 
    text: The best reward I could've ever received.
  withering:
  - speaker: 
    text: The wolf fell without a sound.
  - speaker: 
    text: Then the vines moved. They wrapped around her and pulled her into the flowers.
  - speaker: 
    text: I went in after her.
  - speaker: 
    text: The plant allowed me to enter.
  - speaker: 
    text: But none of us ever came back.
  - speaker: 
    text: Not the same, at least...
  endOfHollowPine:
  - speaker: 
    text: Winter was silent in Hollow Pine.
  - speaker: 
    text: No smoke. No voices. Only flowers, growing through the floorboards.
  - speaker: 
    text: Sometimes, you see one of us walking around.
  - speaker: 
    text: If you see us, if you hear us, stay away.
  - speaker: 
    text: It walks like us, it talks like us, but it's not us.
  - speaker: 
    text: It's not human. It is the forest.
  - speaker: 
    text: And it already knows our scent.
